# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Go stdlib in `lefthook-linux-x64@1.13.6` (a workspace-root devDependency
# pre-built Go binary). Lefthook installs git pre-commit hooks at dev time;
# the binary ends up in `app/node_modules/.pnpm/lefthook-linux-x64@1.13.6/`
# in the capture-worker image because pnpm installs root workspace devDeps
# even with `--filter @furan/capture-worker...`. The capture-worker CMD is
# `node apps/capture-worker/dist/server.js` — it never invokes lefthook,
# the binary sits dormant on disk.
#
# 11 HIGH CVEs flagged by Trivy on the v1.1.1 build (lefthook ships its
# own Go runtime; bumping lefthook itself doesn't necessarily ship a newer
# stdlib until they cut a release built against Go 1.25.10+ / 1.26.3+).
#
# Re-evaluate on every lefthook bump. Permanent fix would be `pnpm prune
# --prod` (or a separate prod-only install stage) before copying node_modules
# into the runtime image — deferred as a Dockerfile cleanup.
#
# Owner: @qasecret-maintainer
# Last reviewed: 2026-05-29 (v1.1.1 build-images run)
CVE-2025-58185
CVE-2025-58186
